From c21fc21d738f11eda1a886a20e39f248d9f686af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (dev box)" <claude@loukdekker.nl>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:03:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(admin): per-title art overrides and admin uploads

Some titles get the wrong automatic art and an admin has no way to fix
it. The Man in the High Castle (tv/62017) has three English logos, all
with zero votes, and the vote-based pick lands on one nobody would choose;
the only remedy today is to wait for TMDB votes to change.

An override pins the art of one title + image kind (+ season/episode for
episode stills, + optionally a request language for posters and logos) to
a TMDB image, a fanart.tv image or an admin upload, and can switch the
rating badges off for it. It is keyed on the resolved title (media type +
TMDB id), never on the requested id, so imdb, tmdb and tvdb requests all
get it.

- Table image_overrides (one additive CREATE TABLE in SCHEMA_SQL), mirrored
  in memory and loaded once: the render path never queries the DB for
  overrides, and with no rows every hook returns its input unchanged, so
  cache keys and output are exactly as before.
- Render paths: the override is applied before the TMDB-vs-fanart
  preference on the poster (incl. the default poster_path), logo, backdrop
  and episode paths, the logo/backdrop refresh path, and therefore also
  with ENABLE_CDN_REDIRECTS and EXTERNAL_CACHE_ONLY. Badges are still
  drawn on top unless the override says no_badges (rendered with limit 0,
  the existing badge-free cache key). A source that cannot be fetched or
  decoded falls back to the automatic art.
- Saving or clearing an override purges the title's cached renders of that
  kind with the existing per-title purge, for every id the title is known
  under (canonical tmdb id, its imdb/tvdb ids, ids in id_cache that resolve
  to it, show art cached under episode ids), and again 60 s later so a
  render that was in flight cannot leave the old art cached.
- Admin API under /api/admin: overrides CRUD, a candidates list (every TMDB
  image in all languages + fanart.tv, with the automatic pick marked),
  raw-body uploads (PNG/JPEG/WebP, sniffed, <= 15 MiB, <= 8000 px, fully
  decoded before they are stored under DB_DIR/uploads/), and a resolve
  route that maps a cached image id to its override key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
